{
  "_comment": [
    "Pages the accessibility and contrast gate (scripts/ui_a11y_scan.js, the",
    "`browser` job in .github/workflows/test.yml) checks in light and dark mode.",
    "Broader than ui_smoke_ci.json on purpose: contrast and naming regressions",
    "land on settings panes, the check-in desk and help as often as on the",
    "match board. Each target costs ~5s across both schemes.",
    "",
    "`a11y.ignore` is for a finding that is wrong, not one that is hard. Each",
    "entry names the rule (an axe rule id, or \"contrast\"), optionally the",
    "target, and says why. See docs/style-guide.md#checking-your-change."
  ],
  "loginAs": "staff_user",
  "tenant": "default",
  "outDir": "/tmp/ui-smoke-ci",
  "a11y": {
    "schemes": ["light", "dark"],
    "ignore": []
  },
  "phone": {
    "_comment": "Layout at phone width: nothing scrolls sideways, runs out of its card or is cut off. Layout does not change with the colour scheme, so one pass is enough. `ignore` takes a CSS selector and a why.",
    "viewport": { "width": 390, "height": 844 },
    "schemes": ["light"],
    "ignore": []
  },
  "targets": [
    { "name": "home-schedule", "path": "/home/schedule" },
    { "name": "home-on-air", "path": "/home/on-air" },
    { "name": "home-player", "path": "/home/player" },
    { "name": "home-profile", "path": "/home/profile" },
